      "metadata": {
        "split_group": "invalid_frivolous_termination"
      },
      "narrative": "The consumer disputed the same mortgage late-payment notation that had been disputed before, but this new packet included a servicer correction letter that had not been supplied in the prior dispute. The letter identified the account, disputed field, and basis. The CRA nevertheless marked the submission as duplicate and frivolous, closed the file without reinvestigation, did not notify the furnisher, did not review the new letter, and sent a closure notice that did not identify missing information. The new letter was dispositive if accepted.\n",
      "provenance": "authored",
      "structured_fields": {},
      "title": "Duplicate termination despite new material proof"
